Regional Capacity Broker does not collect or transmit any telemetry. It makes no
network connection of any kind. Every byte it writes goes to the local store
directory the operator names on the command line or passes to the library, and
nothing leaves the machine running the software.

Regional Capacity Broker accepts contributions from individuals and
organizations on the terms of the Apache License 2.0 without requiring a
Contributor License Agreement (CLA). See CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution
guidance.

Third-party components
----------------------

None. No third-party source code, library, header or generated artefact is
included in, linked into, or required by this product.

The build depends only on the platform's own toolchain and operating system:

  * the C++20 standard library of the toolchain that builds the project;
  * the operating system's file, locking and durability primitives, used for the
    durable journal and snapshot store and for writer fencing
    (FlushFileBuffers and MoveFileEx on Windows, fsync, ftruncate, rename and
    flock elsewhere);
  * the platform thread library, for the bounded worker pool.

SHA-256 and CRC-32C are implemented in this repository from their published
specifications. No cryptographic, compression, serialization or JSON library is
linked, and no package manager is contacted at build time or at run time.

